VI  - 6
IP  - 3
DP  - 2009 May 1
TI  - Innate immunity and asthma.
PG  - 260-5
LID - 10.1513/pats.200807-064RM [doi]
AB  - Asthma remains a major health problem worldwide that has increased in developed 
      countries. Much of the focus in asthma research in the past has been on adaptive, 
      antigen-dependent immune responses. Recent work suggests that the innate, 
      non-antigen-dependent immune system plays a critical role in asthma pathogenesis. 
      Here we will highlight innate receptors and cells in the context of allergic 
      responses. Reviewing animal models and human studies, we focus on interactions of 
      innate and adaptive immunity.
