TI  - Giles f. Filley lecture. Complex systems.
PG  - 467-71
AB  - Physiologic systems in health and disease display an extraordinary range of 
      temporal behaviors and structural patterns that defy understanding based on 
      linear constructs, reductionist strategies, and classical homeostasis. 
      Application of concepts and computational tools derived from the contemporary 
      study of complex systems, including nonlinear dynamics, fractals and "chaos 
      theory," is having an increasing impact on biology and medicine. This 
      presentation provides a brief overview of an emerging area of biomedical 
      research, including recent applications to cardiopulmonary medicine and chronic 
      obstructive lung disease.
