TI  - Progress in chronic obstructive pulmonary disease genetics.
PG  - 405-8
AB  - Familial aggregation of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD) has been 
      demonstrated, suggesting that genetic factors likely influence the variable 
      development of chronic airflow obstruction in response to smoking. A variety of 
      approaches have been used to identify novel COPD susceptibility genes, including 
      association studies, linkage analysis, and rare variant analysis. Future 
      directions for COPD research include genomewide association studies and animal 
      model genetic studies.
