TI  - Regulation of heterotrimeric G protein signaling in airway smooth muscle.
PG  - 47-57
AB  - Heterotrimeric G proteins transduce signals from G protein-coupled receptors to 
      regulate numerous signaling events and functions in airway smooth muscle (ASM). 
      In this article, we detail the function and regulation of heterotrimeric G 
      protein signaling in ASM. We further discuss recent advances in the development 
      of experimental tools in the study of G protein signaling, and speculate how 
      these tools might be used in therapeutic strategies that seek to mitigate 
      bronchospasm and airway remodeling that occur in obstructive airway disease.
