TI  - Exacerbations in chronic obstructive pulmonary disease: do they contribute to 
      disease progression?
PG  - 586-90
AB  - The impact of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD) exacerbations on 
      decline in FEV(1) has been a controversial topic for decades. We will review some 
      of the key studies in this area and discuss potential contributors to 
      inconsistent results of these studies. Dissecting the heterogeneous COPD syndrome 
      into meaningful subtypes and assessing the genetic and environmental influences 
      on COPD-related phenotypes such as exacerbation frequency could clarify the 
      impact of exacerbations on the natural history of COPD.
