DP  - 2012 May
TI  - Chitinase-like proteins in lung injury, repair, and metastasis.
PG  - 57-61
LID - 10.1513/pats.201112-056MS [doi]
AB  - This report explains how our studies of asthma and Th2 inflammation led us to 
      investigate the roles of chitinase-like proteins (CLPs) in lung injury and repair 
      and puts forth an overall hypothesis that can explain the roles that these 
      moieties play in biology and a hypothesis regarding the ways that dysregulated 
      CLP expression may contribute to the pathogenesis of a variety of diseases. We 
      test this hypothesis by assessing the contributions of the CLP breast regression 
      protein (BRP)-39 in the pathogenesis of malignant melanoma metastasis to the 
      lung.
