PG  - 96-102
AB  - Because there are more than one million Americans with HIV, intensive care units 
      continue to see frequent patients with HIV infection. In the era of highly active 
      antiretroviral therapy, clinicians must be aware of drug toxicities and drug 
      interactions. They must also recognize traditional opportunistic infections, as 
      well as newer syndromes such as immune reconstitution syndrome, multicentric 
      Castleman's disease, and primary pleural cell lymphoma.
