TI  - Mesenchymal progenitor cell research: limitations and recommendations.
PG  - 707-10
LID - 10.1513/pats.200801-007AW [doi]
AB  - There is considerable interest in mesenchymal stem cell biology. This relates, in 
      part, to the possibility that such cells could be used to replace tissues in 
      degenerative diseases of mesenchyme. In this article, the current status of the 
      field is discussed, highlighting technical and theoretical issues related to the 
      identification, isolation, and characterization of these cells. Our focus is the 
      endogenous noncirculating mesenchymal stem cell populations that normally reside 
      in adult organs.
